════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 Three Sagas, seven images, one network.

 COMPLETED   — debit, payment, credit
 COMPENSATED — a refusal, and the money given back
 COMPENSATED — a retry ladder climbed to its end, then the same

 Every request entered through the Gateway; no service was called
 directly and no service read another's database — not even the source
 balance, which arrived through a teller's deposit (A-05), not SQL.
 The balances were checked before and after each transfer, so the
 compensation is a fact about the money rather than a status somebody
 wrote down.
